  "text": "France gradually gained control after the changes, rather than improving instantly. Bringing on Kolo Muani and Thuram helped them get a larger share of the passing, but they still produced no shots in the immediate comparison window. [[ev:sb:3869685:1378]] [[ev:sb:3869685:1379]]\n\nThe clearer shift came after Acuña replaced Di María: France’s passing share rose from 53% to 66%, and Argentina stopped producing shots in the next window. [[ev:sb:3869685:2355]] France then introduced Camavinga and Coman, and their pressure eventually became goals through Mbappé’s penalty and equaliser. The changes coincided with the comeback, but the numbers alone cannot prove they caused it. [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]]",
